1
00:05:05,217 --> 00:05:11,217
Single dad, no clue. Single mom, flying solo.

2
00:10:10,434 --> 00:10:16,434
Blended is a comedy, romance film directed by Frank Coraci.

3
00:15:15,652 --> 00:15:21,652
Recently divorced mom Lauren and widowed dad Jim let their friends push
them into a blind date, which goes disastrously wrong.

4
00:20:20,869 --> 00:20:26,869
Unsurprisingly, neither wants to see the other ever again.

5
00:25:26,086 --> 00:25:32,086
However, fate intervenes when both Jim and Lauren, unbeknownst to each other, purchase one-half of
the same vacation package at a South African resort for families, during spring break.

6
00:30:31,304 --> 00:30:37,304
They and their children are forced to share the same romantic suite and
participate in a slew of family activities together.

7
00:35:36,521 --> 00:35:42,521
Jim, played by Adam Sandler.

8
00:40:41,739 --> 00:40:47,739
Lauren, played by Drew Barrymore.

9
00:45:46,956 --> 00:45:52,956
Eddy, played by Kevin Nealon.

10
00:50:52,173 --> 00:50:58,173
Nickens, played by Terry Crews.

11
00:55:57,391 --> 00:56:03,391
Jen, played by Wendi McLendon-Covey.

12
01:01:02,608 --> 01:01:08,608
Hilary, played by Bella Thorne.

13
01:06:07,826 --> 01:06:13,826
Blended is a 2014 American romantic comedy film starring Adam Sandler and Drew Barrymore as two single
parents who went on a blind date together and never wanted to see each other again afterwards.

14
01:11:13,043 --> 01:11:19,043
To their surprise, they both end up at the same African safari resort
with their children and are forced to stay together.

15
01:16:18,260 --> 01:16:24,260
The film was directed by Frank Coraci, and written
by Ivan Menchell and Clare Sera.

16
01:21:23,478 --> 01:21:29,478
The film's ensemble cast also features Kevin Nealon,
Terry Crews, and Wendi McLendon-Covey.

17
01:26:28,695 --> 01:26:34,695
The film was produced by Adam Sandler, Jack Giarraputo, and Mike Karz.

18
01:31:33,913 --> 01:31:39,913
It was released theatrically on May 23, 2014.

19
01:36:39,130 --> 01:36:45,130
grossed $128 million worldwide, against a budget of $40 million, and
received generally negative reviews from critics.

20
01:41:44,347 --> 01:41:50,347
This is the third collaboration between Sandler and Barrymore after The
Wedding Singer (also directed by Coraci) and 50 First Dates.

21
01:46:49,565 --> 01:46:55,565
The film explores themes of single parent, baseball,
extreme sports, safari, south africa.

22
01:51:54,782 --> 01:52:00,782
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
